# .gitignore for viromelib-local  —  ~/Desktop/viromelib/.gitignore
# Revised 2026-10-26. Goal: track code, notebooks and documentation; ignore data, large
# binaries and regenerable figure output.
#


# ── System and editor junk
.DS_Store
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
~$*

# ── Whole trees that are data, not source
data/
work/
libraryDesign/
outputs-sequencefiles/
trash/

# ── Figure inputs and outputs, at ANY depth in EITHER tree.
# Pattern-based rather than enumerated, so it keeps working as figure directories are added
# or renamed. The old file named figures/fig1/inputs and figures/fig1/plots explicitly, which
# stopped covering anything once rank/, representation/, ncbi_virus_space/ and igv/ appeared.
# Directories themselves stay walkable so notebooks beside them remain trackable.
**/inputs/**
**/plots/**
!**/inputs/
!**/plots/
!**/inputs/**/*.md5
!**/plots/**/*.md5
# A figure input manifest IS worth tracking: a clone cannot knit without the inputs, so at
# minimum it should be able to say exactly which files it is missing.

# ── Tabular data and rendered output, globally. All regenerable from a notebook plus inputs.
# NOTE *.txt is global, so plain-text documentation disappears silently. Keep documentation
# in Markdown — *.md is deliberately not ignored anywhere in this file.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.txt
*.tbl
*.json
*.xml
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.html
*.nb.html
*.pdf
*.svg
*.png
*.tiff
*.tif
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.eps
*.ai

# ── Sequence, alignment and interval files
*.fa
*.fasta
*.fa.fai
*.fa.ssi
*.fai
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.bam
*.bam.bai
*.bai
*.sam
*.cram
*.bed
*.gtf
*.bedGraph
*.bw
*.bigWig

# ── Archives and serialised data (these were the real gap: none of the extensions above
# catches an .rds or a .parquet, so they would have been committed silently)
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.gz
*.rds
*.RDS
*.feather
*.parquet
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.npy
*.npz

# ── Kept deliberately: covariance models and alignments are small, versioned inputs that
# define the CM vocabulary (decision 25), so they are NOT ignored above. Listed here only so
# the omission reads as a choice rather than an oversight: *.cm, *.stk, *.sto.
# .gitignore for the flaviLib SUBMODULE  —  ~/Desktop/viromelib/flaviLib/.gitignore
# Revised 2026-10-26.
#
# flaviLib is a git submodule, so it has its own independent tracking and its own ignore rules.
# The parent repo's .gitignore does NOT apply here. This is why `git check-ignore` on a path
# under flaviLib/ from the parent fails with "is in submodule 'flaviLib'".
#
# THE BUG THIS FIXES: the previous version ignored `figures/` wholesale. Inside this submodule
# that means flaviLib/figures/**, so EVERY flaviLib figure notebook was ignored and untrackable.
# Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so `!figures/**/*.Rmd` cannot rescue them —
# the files are unreachable, not merely overridden. Exclude the CONTENTS, never the directory,
# whenever you want to keep some files from inside it.

# ── System and editor junk
.DS_Store
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
~$*

# ── Whole trees that are data, not source
data/
work/
libraryDesign/

# ── figures/: ignore the contents, keep the notebooks, READMEs and input manifests.
# Do NOT replace this block with `figures/` — that was the bug.
figures/**
!figures/**/
!figures/**/*.Rmd
!figures/**/*.rmd
!figures/**/*.R
!figures/**/*.md
!figures/**/*.md5

# ── Figure inputs and outputs at any depth. Pattern-based so it keeps working as figure
# directories are added or renamed (rank/, input_distribution/, representation/,
# mg_dependence/, vintage_75x75/ all appeared after the old rules were written).
**/inputs/**
**/plots/**
!**/inputs/
!**/plots/
!**/inputs/**/*.md5
!**/plots/**/*.md5

# ── Tabular data and rendered output, globally. Regenerable from a notebook plus its inputs.
# *.md is deliberately never ignored: keep documentation in Markdown, not .txt.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.txt
*.tbl
*.json
*.xml
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.html
*.nb.html
*.pdf
*.svg
*.png
*.tiff
*.tif
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.eps
*.ai

# ── Sequence, alignment and interval files
*.fa
*.fasta
*.fa.fai
*.fa.ssi
*.fai
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.bam
*.bam.bai
*.bai
*.sam
*.cram
*.bed
*.gtf
*.bedGraph
*.bw
*.bigWig

# ── Archives and serialised data. None of the extensions above catches an .rds or .parquet,
# so without these they would be committed silently.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.gz
*.rds
*.RDS
*.feather
*.parquet
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.npy
*.npz

# ── NOT ignored, deliberately: *.cm, *.stk, *.sto. Covariance models and alignments are small
# versioned inputs that define the CM vocabulary (decision 25); without them under version
# control, no figure's CM classes are reproducible.